# {name} — Getting Started

> Scaffolded with `projio init --profile sirota`. This doc lives under
> `.projio/` so your project's top-level `README.md` stays yours to write.

## Project structure

```
{name}/
  .projio/          # projio workspace config, render settings, subsystem state
                    # (this file lives here)
  bib/              # bibliography: srcbib/ (Zotero exports), articles/ (PDFs)
  code/
    lib/            # shared code libraries (datalad subdatasets)
    pipelines/      # Snakemake flows (one dir per flow)
    scripts/        # standalone scripts
    utils/          # project-specific cross-flow utilities
  docs/             # MkDocs site source
    log/            # project notes (ideas, issues, decisions)
    plan/           # research questions and milestones (generated from plan/)
    pipelines/      # auto-generated pipeline documentation
    manuscript/     # paper sections
    infra/          # infrastructure notes
    deliverables/   # final outputs
  plan/             # questio YAML sources (questions.yml, milestones.yml)
```

## Next steps

### 1. Install input datasets

```bash
conda run -n labpy datalad install -d . -s <source_url> data/<dataset_name>
```

### 2. Clone shared code libraries

```bash
conda run -n labpy datalad install -d . -s <lab_gitlab>/cogpy code/lib/cogpy
conda run -n labpy datalad install -d . -s <lab_gitlab>/labpy code/lib/labpy
```

### 3. Set up the Python environment

Overlay a project venv on top of the shared conda base:

```bash
conda activate cogpy
python -m venv .venv --system-site-packages
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e code/lib/cogpy -e code/lib/labpy
python -m ipykernel install --user --name {name}
```

### 4. Register code libraries

```bash
projio sync   # auto-discovers code/lib/* and code/utils/
```

### 5. Define research questions

Edit `plan/questions.yml` and `plan/milestones.yml`, then ask the agent:

- "What are my open research questions?" (`questio_status`)
- "What's the next step?" (use `/questio-next` skill)

## Lab siblings

The sirota profile pre-configures two datalad siblings for lab
infrastructure. Both use `projio sibling` — preview-first; add `--yes` to
actually run.

### GitLab — code + history

Pushes land under the `sirotalab/` group:

```bash
projio sibling gitlab           # preview
projio sibling gitlab --yes     # create
datalad push --to gitlab        # push commits
```

The target project path is `sirotalab/{name}`. Change it by editing
`helpers.sibling.gitlab.project_template` in `.projio/config.yml`.

### RIA store — full dataset backup

The lab RIA store lives at `/storage/share/git/ria-store`. The sirota profile
creates a sibling named `ria-storage` with alias `{name}`:

```bash
projio sibling ria              # preview (shows resolved alias + store)
projio sibling ria --yes        # create
datalad push --to ria-storage   # push annex + git
```

**Alias safety:** projio refuses to create the sibling if the alias is
already bound to a different dataset in the store. If you see an `[ABORT]`
message, either pick a different `project_name` in `.projio/config.yml`, or
pass `--force-alias` — only when you genuinely mean to replace a stale
entry.

## Working with projio through an agent

Projio is designed to be driven through an AI agent (Claude Code). The agent
has access to all projio tools via MCP. Common workflows:

| Task | What to ask the agent |
|------|----------------------|
| Add a paper          | "ingest this DOI into the bibliography" |
| Create a pipeline    | "create a new flow called preprocessing" |
| Write a notebook     | "create a notebook in the preprocessing flow" |
| Run a pipeline       | "run the preprocessing flow" |
| Build docs           | "build and serve the docs site" |
| Capture a note       | "log an issue about X" |
| Search the project   | "search for references about Y" |

## Conda environments

This project uses three conda environments:

| Environment | Purpose |
|-------------|---------|
| `cogpy`  | Data analysis, Snakemake, notebooks |
| `projio` | Projio tools, MkDocs, MCP server |
| `labpy`  | DataLad and git-annex operations |

The generated `.projio/projio.mk` maps these to make variables automatically.
